WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:07.398
An ESD kit only protects you if every link in the chain is connected.

00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:09.895
Miss one, and it is just a grey mat.

00:00:10.495 --> 00:00:15.607
The most common ESD failure is simple: the strap is worn but not clipped in,

00:00:15.607 --> 00:00:18.634
or the mat cord was never plugged into earth.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.279
Here is the chain.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:24.931
The ESD mat has a press stud; snap the grounding cord onto it.

00:00:25.211 --> 00:00:27.507
Connect that cord to the 3-way connector.

00:00:27.787 --> 00:00:30.453
Connect your wrist strap cord to the same connector.

00:00:30.733 --> 00:00:34.152
Then connect the grounding plug to your facility's earth point.

00:00:34.432 --> 00:00:38.026
Wear the strap snug against bare skin before touching any part.

00:00:38.306 --> 00:00:42.884
Keep plastic bags, foam and paper off the mat, because they hold static.

00:00:43.484 --> 00:00:48.563
Every Furnisys ESD kit includes the wrist strap, grounding cords, buttons,

00:00:48.563 --> 00:00:53.505
grounding plug and 3-way connector, so the whole chain arrives together.

00:00:54.105 --> 00:00:56.277
Check the chain at the start of every shift.

00:00:56.557 --> 00:00:57.960
Does your team check theirs?

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.515
Comment below, and next, learn why ESD protection should go from bench to floor.

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:08.360
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

